        "header": "Abstract",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.10060/2609.10060v1/fig1.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Overview of our bias evaluation pipeline.We use relative representations to project the hidden spaces of the fine-tuned model (ℳaud\\mathcal{M}_{\\mathrm{aud}}) and the reference (base) model (ℳref\\mathcal{M}_{\\mathrm{ref}}) into a shared space via anchor sentences. Within this shared space, we calculate distances between target representations and sets of positive and negative sentences.\nBy comparing these distances (Δ​B\\Delta B),our method can, for example, detect potential side-effects induced during fine-tuning without the need for curated datasets, by determining whetherℳaud\\mathcal{M}_{\\mathrm{aud}}exhibits greater bias toward target groups thanℳref\\mathcal{M}_{\\mathrm{ref}}.",
                "position": 315
            }
        ]
